  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "The moment you sign a loan, it begins a journey you never see. Here's how your debt gets sold, step by step.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "bank",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "loop"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Your loan's",
            "secret journey."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "First you borrow. Then the bank bundles your loan with thousands of others. Then it's sliced into bonds and sold to investors worldwide.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "rows",
          "kicker": "The chain of ownership",
          "rows": [
            {
              "rank": "1",
              "name": "You borrow",
              "value": "→",
              "note": "sign the loan",
              "color": "#1f7a3d",
              "bar": 0.3
            },
            {
              "rank": "2",
              "name": "Bundled",
              "value": "→",
              "note": "with thousands more",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.6
            },
            {
              "rank": "3",
              "name": "Sliced into bonds",
              "value": "→",
              "note": "sold to investors",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.85
            },
            {
              "rank": "4",
              "name": "Owned globally",
              "value": "✓",
              "note": "pensions, funds",
              "color": "#c0392b",
              "bar": 1.0
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Turning those bundled loans into tradable securities is securitization.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-sec",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · securitization"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Those slices get sold as bonds, each one a claim on a piece of your monthly payment.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "bonds",
          "label": "claims on your payments",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A bond is just a tradable promise of future payments.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-bond",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · bond"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Multiply that across every loan in the economy, and debt itself becomes the main product.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Debt is the product",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "loop"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That creeping dominance of finance has a name, financialization.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-finz",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · financialization"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "By the end of the chain, almost nobody who owns your loan has ever met you.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Strangers own it",
          "props": [
            "globe",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And compounding quietly makes that stream of your payments even more valuable.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-compound",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · compound interest"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
